### 2d. The dated errata beside the table-1 files (new files)

# PRETABLE.errata.md -- corrections to ../table1_20261105/PRETABLE.out (#575 ppccrandcorc), dated 2026-11-05 (round 2)

PRETABLE.out is a historical record and is NOT rewritten; its timestamps stand.  The corrections below come from pass 2
(p2_20261105/codex_codex_r575_p2.txt F4, F5, F7 and section 3; p2_20261105/ollama_glm.txt section 3) and were checked against
table1/SCORES.txt, the file mtimes and the simulator r2_20261105/v575b.py (`errata62').

#### F4 -- the absent-binary null medium

exec
"C:\\WINDOWS\\System32\\WindowsPowerShell\\v1.0\\powershell.exe" -Command '$p = Get-Content -LiteralPath '"'C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/_scratchpad/cloud_r3/P3_R575_CODEX.md'; "'$p[360..539]' in C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL
 succeeded in 120ms:

PRETABLE.out lines 5-6 say: "Null media (/bin/true, an absent binary, /bin/false): CONTROL=FAIL."

Correction: /bin/true (5/62) and /bin/false (1/62) score CONTROL=FAIL.  An absent binary does NOT reach a CONTROL record: the
probe's first `subprocess.run` raises FileNotFoundError before any row (table1/probe_null_absent.out, last line), so there is no
RESULT, no CONTROL and no sentinel.  SCORES.txt line 4 records it correctly: `null_absent [62 rows] none CONTROL=none DONE=0`.  The
gate's first check (the completion sentinel) is what reds it.

#### F5 -- "its mtime precedes every file in table1/"

PRETABLE.out lines 1-2 say: "Written BEFORE table 1 runs (its mtime precedes every file in table1/)."

Correction: one file in table1/ is older.  table1/probe62_frozen.py was copied first (2026-11-05 01:36:56.192 local, 07:36:56.192Z);
PRETABLE.out was written 86 ms later (01:36:56.278 local, 07:36:56.278Z).  Every other file in table1/ (MD5.txt 01:37:08 onward,
SCORES.txt 01:38:59) is later than PRETABLE.out.  The claim that matters -- the predictions were written before any variant was
built or run -- holds.  table1/VERDICT.md line 6 already states this exception.

#### F7 -- "rows reading the debugger ... are predicted green on every variant"

PRETABLE.out lines 3-4 say: "rows reading the debugger, the disassembler or mfcr are predicted green on every variant."

Correction: every semantic row reads CR through the debugger too (the probe seeds CR with `cr=' and reads it back with `reg'), and
PRETABLE's own HEAD prediction lists ten of them red.  The sentence meant the APPARATUS CONTROLS: `ctl session`, `ctl live`,
`ctl seed holds`, `ctl cr seed`, `ctl mfcr`, `neg apparatus`, and the `* session`, `* mfcr` and `* disasm` rows of each table session
(no variant of either table touches the debugger, the disassembler or mfcr).  The `* others` rows are COMPUTED, not assumed green:
t1/t2 red `64 others`, `32 others` and `edge others`.  r2_20261105/PRETABLE_2.out uses the corrected wording.

#### The four R5 bt-substitution predictions the pass-1 ruling required (predicted, not built)

adj_p1_20261105/MYTHOS_local.md R5: "Clause 2 bt-substitutions (`bt & !bb`, `ba & !bt`, `bt | !bb`, `ba | !bt`) each red an
existing row by enumeration ...; list them in PRETABLE as predicted, not built."  PRETABLE.out omitted them.  Their exact red sets on
the 62 rows, computed by r2_20261105/v575b.py (`errata62'; the same simulator reproduces table 1's 17 legs exactly):

    r5a crandc `if (bt & !bb)`   3 red: 64_crandc_10, 64_crandc_hi, 32_crandc_10
    r5b crandc `if (ba & !bt)`   3 red: 64_crandc_10, 64_crandc_hi, 32_crandc_10
    r5c crorc  `if (bt | !bb)`   3 red: 64_crorc_01,  64_crorc_hi,  32_crorc_01
    r5d crorc  `if (ba | !bt)`   2 red: 64_crorc_00,  32_crorc_00

(Here `bt` is the BT field index, 0..31: `bt & !bb` is bt's low bit when b = 0 -- 0 for BT 10 and 20, red where the want is 1;
`!bt` is 1 only at BT = 0, which no crandc/crorc truth or hi row uses, so `ba & !bt` is 0 and `ba | !bt` is a.)  codex's pass-2
derivation (section 3) lists the same four sets.  The ruling's parenthetical "the owed rows stay green under all nine" is also
false: `64 crandc hi` / `64 crorc hi` are red under c and under d1-d4 (SCORES.txt lines 8-12), as table 1 measured and VERDICT.md
reports; see table1/VERDICT.errata.md.  Their red sets on the round-2 66 rows are in r2_20261105/PRETABLE_2.out ("PREDICTED ONLY").

#### VERDICT.errata.md -- correction to VERDICT.md (#575 ppccrandcorc, table 1), dated 2026-11-05 (round 2)

VERDICT.md is a historical record and is NOT rewritten.  The correction comes from pass 2 (p2_20261105/codex_codex_r575_p2.txt F6)
and was checked against adj_p1_20261105/MYTHOS_local.md (the R5 table) and SCORES.txt.

#### F6 -- "the four the ruling listed per variant"

VERDICT.md lines 12-13 say: "d1-d6 (operand complement moved, dropped, operator crossed) -- 5 each, the four the ruling listed
per variant plus a hi row on d1-d4".

Correction: the pass-1 ruling's R5 table did not list four rows for every d variant.  It listed FOUR for d1-d4 (64/32 crandc 01, 10;
64/32 crorc 01, 10; 64/32 crandc 10, 11; 64/32 crorc 00, 01) and FIVE for d5 and d6 (64/32 crandc 00, 11 plus edge crandc bt0;
64/32 crorc 00, 11 plus edge crorc bt31).  The measured 5-each (SCORES.txt lines 9-14) therefore decomposes as:

    d1-d4: the ruling's four rows plus that handler's `hi` row (the ruling wrote the table before the hi rows existed, and its
           parenthetical "the owed rows stay green under all nine" is false for c and d1-d4 -- SCORES.txt lines 8-12);
    d5-d6: the ruling's five rows, unchanged (the hi rows stay green: (1,0) and (0,1) are not fixed points of the crossed
           operator for the 00/11 cells, but the hi inputs (1,0) -> 1|!0 = 1 and (0,1) -> 0&!1 = 0 equal the wants).

Nothing else in VERDICT.md changes: 15 of 15 variants red, 17 of 17 legs exactly as predicted, the null-media and HEAD lines stand.

## 3. CLOSURE.md (the enumeration, its denominator, the misses, the equivalents, the new rows)

# #575 ppccrandcorc -- CLASS CLOSURE BY SIMULATION (round 2, 2026-11-05)

Simulator: r2_20261105/v575b.py (table1_20261105/v575.py extended; `v575b.py check62' re-derives table 1's 17 predictions
on the old 62 rows and matches PRETABLE.out exactly).  Handlers simulated statement by statement:
src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr.c X(crandc) :2729-2737 and X(crorc) :2756-2764; dispatch :4638 and :4641.

ENUMERATION (one edit per cell, per handler): field mask m in 0..30 at BT, BA, BB (3 x 31); each source read taking another
field's index (BA<-BB, BA<-BT, BB<-BA, BB<-BT); the read mask `& 1' widened to `& 3' and `& 7' at BA and at BB; the clear moved
before the reads, deleted, or replaced by a toggle; the set deleted or `|=' -> `^='; the condition edits table 1 had (b, d-moved,
d-dropped, d-crossed) plus the pass-1 ruling's four R5 bt-substitutions and the identity body; the dispatch case bound to each
of the six other CR-logical handlers; and table 1's c (both bodies identity).

DENOMINATOR: 239 cells = 6 clear + 15 cond + 12 decode + 186 mask + 8 read + 8 rmask + 4 set.
[the CELL -> ROW MAP table, 43502 bytes, omitted here: GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/ppccrandcorc/r2_20261105/CLOSURE.md]

MISSED BY THE 62 ROWS (25 cells):
  - crandc BB mask &5
  - crandc BB mask &9
  - crandc BB mask &11
  - crandc BB mask &13
  - crandc BB mask &17
  - crandc BB mask &19
  - crandc BB mask &21
  - crandc BB mask &23
  - crandc BB mask &25
  - crandc BB mask &27
  - crandc BB mask &29
  - crandc BB read <- BT index
  - crandc BA read mask &3
  - crandc BA read mask &7
  - crandc BB read mask &3
  - crandc BB read mask &7
  - crandc clear moved before the reads
  - crandc clear -> toggle (^=)
  - crandc set |= -> ^=
  - crorc BA mask &29
  - crorc BB mask &29
  - crorc BB read <- BT index
  - crorc clear moved before the reads
  - crorc clear -> toggle (^=)
  - crorc set |= -> ^=

EQUIVALENT (4 cells; proved, not merely unobserved):
  - crandc BA read mask &3: `ba & !bb' is a bitwise AND with !bb in {0,1}: only bit 0 of ba (= CR[BA]) can survive
  - crandc BA read mask &7: same: (ba & !bb) != 0  <=>  (ba & 1) && !bb
  - crandc set |= -> ^=: the clear at :2734 has just zeroed the bit, so ^= and |= set it alike
  - crorc set |= -> ^=: the clear at :2761 has just zeroed the bit, so ^= and |= set it alike

EXCLUDED (1 cells):
  - crandc clear -> toggle (^=): disclosed in the probe's clause (e)(5): every crandc row with result 0 pre-sets the inverse

STILL UNDETECTED BY THE 66 ROWS (0 cells):

NEW ROWS (4; single-instruction sessions shaped like the `hi' rows):
  64 crandc bbmask  crandc BT=16 BA=5 BB=31 seed=0xfffffffe want=1  CR[BT] pre-set EQUAL to the result (1)
  64 crandc order   crandc BT=9 BA=5 BB=9 seed=0x04400000 want=0  CR[BT] pre-set inverse (1)
  64 crorc bamask   crorc BT=16 BA=31 BB=5 seed=0xffff7ffe want=0  CR[BT] pre-set EQUAL to the result (0)
  64 crorc bbmask   crorc BT=31 BA=5 BB=31 seed=0x00000001 want=0  CR[BT] pre-set inverse (1)

WHY THESE FOUR AND NO FEWER.  A source-site row detects mask m iff CR[x & m] != CR[x] with the other operand decisive; with
x = 31 every m in 0..30 is an alias, so one row per site with CR[0..30] uniformly opposite to CR[31] closes the whole site.
crandc BB needs a = 1 and CR[0..30] = 1, CR[31] = 0 (want 1): pre-setting CR[BT] EQUAL to the result keeps the uniform seed
and makes the same row read CR[BT] = 1 != CR[BB] = 0 for the BB<-BT cell (an inverse pre-set hides BB<-BT on every row, as
codex B1-B2 show).  crandc clear-before-read needs BT == BB with b = 1 (want 0), a different seed: its own row (BT == BA is
invisible for crandc: a is forced to 1-want, and the early clear changes a only when b = 1, where the result is 0 either
way).  crorc BA needs b = 1, CR[0..30] = 1, CR[31] = 0 (want 0); pre-setting CR[BT] = 0 EQUAL to the result makes it read
CR[BT] = 0 != CR[BB] = 1 for BB<-BT, and incidentally sees the crorc toggle (a 0 result pre-set 0).  Its one blind alias
(m = 16 = BT) is red on `64 crorc 11' (BA 1 -> 0).  crorc BB needs a = 0, CR[0..30] = 0, CR[31] = 1 (want 0): with BT = BB = 31
the inverse pre-set IS CR[31] = 1, and the same row is the crorc clear-before-read pin.  The two crandc needs (want 1 uniform
ones; BT == BB with b = 1) and the two crorc needs (uniform ones; uniform zeros) are pairwise incompatible seeds, so four rows
is the minimum for single-instruction sessions.

OLD rows: 62.  NEW rows: 4 (N = 66).

